# Always rebuild the launcher after updates

Whenever you finish an AquaTech update that players/clients should get — mods, kubejs, configs, launcher code, icons, sync logic, or `publish_client_pack` — **always rebuild and deploy the launcher before ending the task**.

## Required steps (do not skip)

1. If pack content changed: run `python tools/publish_client_pack.py` (or at least sync jars + `manifest.json` into `dist/AquaTech-Client` and `dist/releases/AquaTech-Client`).
2. Rebuild the **onedir** bundle (faster cold start than onefile):
   ```powershell
   python -m PyInstaller --noconfirm --clean AquaTechLauncher.spec
   Remove-Item dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
   Copy-Item dist\AquaTechLauncher dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher -Recurse -Force
   Compress-Archive -Path dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher\* -DestinationPath dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher.zip -Force
   ```
3. Confirm `dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher\AquaTechLauncher.exe` has a fresh timestamp.
4. Tell the user the launcher was rebuilt and where it is (`dist\releases\AquaTechLauncher\` or the zip). Friends run the `.exe` inside the folder (do not ship a lone onefile exe).

## Do not

- End a client-facing update with only source/`server/mods` changes and an old exe.
- Assume a cached PyInstaller build is enough — use `--clean` when unsure.
- Go back to onefile unless explicitly requested (onefile re-extracts to TEMP every launch → Defender → very slow).
